1
00:05:06,315 --> 00:05:12,315
The ball is back!

2
00:10:12,631 --> 00:10:18,631
Phantasm II is a action, horror, science fiction
film directed by Don Coscarelli.

3
00:15:18,947 --> 00:15:24,947
Mike, after his release from a psychiatric hospital, teams up with his old
pal Reggie to hunt down the Tall Man, who is at it again.

4
00:20:25,263 --> 00:20:31,263
A mysterious, beautiful girl has also become part of Mike's dreams,
and they must find her before the Tall Man does.

5
00:25:31,578 --> 00:25:37,578
Mike, played by James LeGros.

6
00:30:37,894 --> 00:30:43,894
Reggie, played by Reggie Bannister.

7
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:50,210
The Tall Man, played by Angus Scrimm.

8
00:40:50,526 --> 00:40:56,526
Liz, played by Paula Irvine.

9
00:45:56,842 --> 00:46:02,842
Alchemy, played by Samantha Phillips.

10
00:51:03,157 --> 00:51:09,157
Father Meyers, played by Kenneth Tigar.

11
00:56:09,473 --> 00:56:15,473
Phantasm II is a 1988 American science fantasy horror film written and directed by Don
Coscarelli and stars Angus Scrimm, James LeGros, and Reggie Bannister.

12
01:01:15,789 --> 01:01:21,789
It is a sequel to Phantasm (1979) and is the second
installment in the Phantasm franchise.

13
01:06:22,105 --> 01:06:28,105
The plot follows the first film's protagonist, Mike Pearson, who is recently released from a mental
institution, recruits his friend Reggie and some new friends in an effort to defeat the Tall Man.

14
01:11:28,421 --> 01:11:34,421
The film caused controversy among fans by recasting main character
Mike with LeGros, and was not well received by critics.

15
01:16:34,736 --> 01:16:40,736
It was followed by two direct-to-video sequels: Phantasm III: Lord of the Dead (1994) and Phantasm IV: Oblivion (1998) as well
as the final film in the Phantasm franchise: Phantasm: Ravager (2016), which received a theatrical release.

16
01:21:41,052 --> 01:21:47,052
Following distribution problems in the U.S., Phantasm II was released
in Region 1 on DVD in 2009 and Blu-ray disc in 2013.

17
01:26:47,368 --> 01:26:53,368
The film explores themes of portal, undertaker, evil, tall man, sentinals.

18
01:31:53,684 --> 01:31:59,684
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
